                <pb facs="0599" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg515"/>

                <head>No. 262.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Boutelle.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department, of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-07-15"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 15,
                        1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have your letter dated yesterday
                    enclosing the affidavit of Stephen R. Balkam, relating the circumstances of his
                    being ordered away from St. Andrews, New Brunswick, by the Dominion cruiser
                    Middleton, Captain Kent, in July 9th instant, and the refusal by Captain Kent to
                    allow thq deponent to purchase fish caught and sold by Canadians for
                    canning.</p>
                <p>The affidavit shall be placed on file for reference.</p>
                <p>Yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
